Error [E2302]: the `ref` field `name` would point at something that dies first
  --> tests/ui/ref_field_dangles_local.jet:7:30
    |
  7 |     val h: Holder = Holder { name: local };
    |                              ^^^^
 Why: a `ref` field stores a view, not its own copy, so its source has to outlive the struct — but the local `local` doesn't live long enough to promise that here
 Fix: store an owned value: drop `ref` so the struct keeps its own copy (or `.clone()` into it)
